# Build context rules shared by every image built from this directory:
#   Dockerfile       development (production target) and test targets
#   Dockerfile.oprf  OPRF sidecars
#   Dockerfile.prod  production api and web targets. It copies all of
#                    packages/ (client sources included) plus
#                    deploy/entrypoint.sh, docker-compose.prod.yml,
#                    deploy/caddy/Caddyfile and static/apex.html.
# A pattern without a leading **/ matches at the context root only, so
# anything that must stay out of nested package directories needs that form.

# Dependencies rebuilt inside container (matches nested dirs too)
# (packages/*/node_modules has pnpm symlinks with host-absolute paths).
**/node_modules

# All hidden files and directories (3+ chars) - none needed at runtime
# Covers: .git, .github, .vscode, .lh, .editorconfig, .npmrc, .nvmrc,
#         .prettierignore, .browserslistrc, .eslintcache, .svelte-kit, etc.
.??*
!.env.example
!.dockerignore

# Environment files - NEVER bake secrets into image layers
.env
.env.*
*.local
# Nested copies: Dockerfile.prod copies the whole packages/ tree.
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Local TLS material (mkcert dev certificates live in packages/client/.certs).
**/.certs
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Build artifacts and caches
dist
coverage
build
# Host build outputs inside packages; the prod builder regenerates them.
packages/*/build
packages/*/dist
**/.svelte-kit

# IDE and editor
*.swp
*.swo

# Tooling config (not needed at runtime)
lefthook.yml
commitlint.config.*
eslint.config.*
vitest.config.*
# tsconfig.base.json # needed by tsx for TypeScript resolution (Dockerfile COPY)

# Documentation (not needed at runtime)
docs
*.md
!packages/*/README.md
LICENSE
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES

# Test files (not needed at runtime)
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/__tests__

# Static demo site, built and published separately and never part of an
# image. The prod builder's first install sees only the four packages whose
# manifests it copies; its production reinstall must see the same set.
packages/demo
